WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.410
Donald Trump has announced a new policy for
the Corona virus bailouts.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:08.730
That is exactly the type of so-called socialism.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.629
Note that I use the word so-called that he
promised us multiple times now that this country

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:16.330
would never, ever, ever do.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:20.160
Trump announced it via Twitter, of course,
saying that, quote, Starting early next week

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:26.759
at my order, the United States will be purchasing
from our farmers, ranchers and specialty crop

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:27.960
growers.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:36.310
Three billion dollars worth of dairy, meat
and produce for food lines and kitchens.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.700
Farmers to family, food box.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.610
Great news for all.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.830
There are so many things here to talk about
and to deal with.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.870
So first of all, yeah, if you have not heard
about this, that we have food lines here in

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:52.030
the United States and they're growing and
they're huge.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.030
All right.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:59.410
The number of people lining up at food banks
waiting hours outdoors in the heat, waiting

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.260
to get food.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.650
And also at certain non-profits and other
organizations that are doing these food boxes

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.100
either for free or heavily discounted.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.360
This is what people like Trump often say.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.700
You would only see in socialist or communist
countries.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.700
But it's happening here.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.540
It's happening here in the United States.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.360
It's been happening, but it's happening even
more acutely because of Corona virus.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.600
That's number one.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.740
These are the bread lines that Don Junior
and others decried and announced.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.860
We would never have this in the United States.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:31.120
Just months ago, they said it.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.120
It's here.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.560
It's been here, but now it's here even more
strongly.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.330
Number two, one could argue that this is even
more than just a socialist idea.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:44.571
Trump is coming up with I'm not going to call
it communist, but certainly we could be talking

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:45.840
about state socialism.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:52.560
The government will become the buyer from
people who who raise food manufacturer, raise

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.900
grow food.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.490
They are going to be the buyer, the government,
and they are going to be doing that to keep

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.970
the company afloat.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:09.139
And they are going to redistribute those resources
to people who cannot afford them or who don't

00:02:09.139 --> 00:02:10.459
have food to eat.

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:15.099
Now, remember, Trump has said many times we're
never going to be a socialist country.

00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:16.790
Here's one example from the United Nations.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:22.870
Today, I repeat a message for the world that
I have delivered at home.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.609
America will never be a socialist country.

00:02:25.609 --> 00:02:33.069
In the last century, socialism and communism
killed 100 million people.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.370
Now, of course, I want to be really clear.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.299
I'm not telling you that this policy is necessarily
a bad idea given where we are today.

00:02:40.299 --> 00:02:42.669
Obviously, preventing it would have been much
smarter.

00:02:42.669 --> 00:02:45.670
I am not here to tell you that we are now
a socialist country.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.609
I am also not a socialist.

00:02:47.609 --> 00:02:55.510
What I am telling you is that this alpha pull
yourself up by your bootstraps ideology very

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:59.080
quickly changes when things get tough.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:04.169
And this is exactly the critique of capitalism
that a social Democrat like me has been making

00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:05.169
for years.

00:03:05.169 --> 00:03:06.540
We had been listen.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.739
Of course.

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:09.230
Inequality has been huge.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:13.889
Wages have been relatively stagnant for decades
by a whole bunch of measures.

00:03:13.889 --> 00:03:18.340
Two months ago, we had a solid economy again
by the measures that are typically used.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.790
We can argue whether it's thanks to Trump
or not.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.629
I think mostly it's not thanks to Trump.

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:23.999
But we had low unemployment.

00:03:23.999 --> 00:03:25.419
We had a high stock market.

00:03:25.419 --> 00:03:27.359
We had appropriate inflation rate.

00:03:27.359 --> 00:03:28.739
We had high consumer confidence.

00:03:28.739 --> 00:03:32.889
Wages were ticking up despite not not being
anything too dramatic.

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:34.790
Yes, of course, too much poverty.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.029
We had hunger, inequality.

00:03:36.029 --> 00:03:37.029
I get it.

00:03:37.029 --> 00:03:41.959
But compared to lots of times past and many
other countries, things we're doing OK.

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:42.959
Two months ago.

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:47.610
So the lesson is look at how quickly we now
have 15 percent unemployment potentially going

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.730
to 20 percent.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:53.859
And how quickly we have explosive food lines
that are hours long and how quickly we have

00:03:53.859 --> 00:03:58.579
the government buying food from farmers to
redistribute to people who can't afford it.

00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:01.680
This is not about we should be a socialist
country.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:08.379
It's just a reminder that the U.S. has had
socialism when it's convenient for a long

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:12.219
time, when there are calamities, when you
need to bail out an industry with companies

00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:16.419
that are too big to fail while you'll apply
socialism, there need to spread the costs

00:04:16.419 --> 00:04:20.379
out of fixing the environmental damage done
by industry.

00:04:20.379 --> 00:04:21.379
Socialized the.

00:04:21.379 --> 00:04:24.650
Cleanup, capitalism for the profits, socialism
for the cost.

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:29.770
If you have a virus that you mishandled leading
to an even worse economic implosion than we

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:30.900
would otherwise have had.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.710
Well, just start buying food and giving it
to people in food lines.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:39.470
So the solution here is we should be dealing
with the fragility of the system in a proactive

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:45.420
way instead of reacting in what is a completely
impotent way.

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.420
That is the problem.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:54.970
And the point of social democracy is you take
capitalism, but you commit money to proactively

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:58.530
insulating the system from shocks and calamities.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.909
Free market capitalism, by its nature, doesn't
do proactive.

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:03.909
It does.

00:05:03.909 --> 00:05:04.909
It's just not in there.

00:05:04.909 --> 00:05:05.909
It's too expensive.

00:05:05.909 --> 00:05:06.909
It's not immediately beneficial.

00:05:06.909 --> 00:05:11.139
True free market capitalism would not do the
proactive stuff.

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:15.669
That's why you need the regulatory framework
of social democracy.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:19.380
And again, this isn't the type of stuff Trump
said we would never have here.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.310
And he's doing it and he's right to do it.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:22.689
I want to be clear.

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:23.689
It's the right.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:27.310
It's one of the right policies given what's
going on.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:32.139
The logistical and crony istick elements of
it will, of course, be a disaster, as it always

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:33.460
is the case for Trump.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:38.440
But the point is their principles evaporate
when they have a situation like this to deal

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:38.449
with.

